+## 2026-09-20 - React Array Sort Memoization
+**Learning:** In large React components, complex sorting operations (like those using `.sort()` on arrays of objects) trigger on every render if not memoized, causing unnecessary CPU cycles even when unrelated state changes. 
+**Action:** Always wrap `.sort()` calculations in `useMemo` hooks, especially when rendering lists or tables. Ensure to include the underlying array and all sort criteria in the dependency array to maintain accurate state without re-evaluating unnecessarily.
